WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.980
A blink and you'll miss it "Black Panther"-related
cameo in "Thor 4" could have massive story

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.770
ramifications for Phase 4 of the MCU.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:13.520
Keep watching for the major Black Panther
cameo you probably missed in "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.104
Warning! Spoilers ahead.

00:00:15.104 --> 00:00:19.289
"Thor: Love and Thunder" is out in theaters
now, and the titular hero is up against a

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:20.289
new foe.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:25.890
Gorr the God Butcher is on a mission to kill
all gods across the universe, a ruthless rampage

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.060
that leads him to the shores of New Asgard.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.630
While Gorr's actions threaten to usher in
a new age of chaos, Thor is faced with the

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:38.110
return of his ex-girlfriend, Dr. Jane Foster,
who now bears the mantle of "The Mighty Thor."

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.999
It's a complicated time for the God of Thunder.

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:43.219
"Jane?!"

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.120
One of the film's core strengths is that it
explores the mysterious lives of the gods

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.080
and goddesses that populate the mythologies
of various cultures.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.940
Although we've seen Norse gods like Odin,
Loki, and Frigga, the latest "Thor" franchise

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:02.890
installment introduces viewers to a variety
of deities in Omnipotent City, a gilded temple

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:07.280
where gods can partake in heavenly debauchery
away from the woes of mankind.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.219
The star-studded lineup of deities is key
to the plot, but also provides the opportunity

00:01:12.219 --> 00:01:16.190
for levity within a narrative that's as serious
as it is silly.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:20.780
Some of the faces of the gods are more recognizable
than others, including one figure who should

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.469
be familiar to fans of the MCU.

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:27.149
With Gorr in possession of the Necrosword,
our heroes know that they'll need to raise

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:31.900
a formidable army to defeat him and ensure
the safe return of Asgard's youth.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.659
To accomplish that goal, Thor, Jane, Valkyrie,
and Korg hitch up a converted amusement park

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:40.070
ride and head to Omnipotent City.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:44.359
While Thor tries to iron out a deal with the
inevitably pompous Zeus, viewers are privy

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:49.825
to a glimpse at the gods and goddesses assembled,
including the exceedingly adorable God of Dumplings.

00:01:49.825 --> 00:01:55.200
However, there's an even more interesting
idol in attendance: The panther goddess Bast,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.149
whose lore is extremely important to the "Black
Panther'' franchise.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:04.399
Although Bast only appears in flashback as
a shadowy feline figure in the 2018 solo film

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:09.409
starring Chadwick Boseman, viewers finally
get to see the goddess in full physical form

00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:11.319
in "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:16.409
Played by actress and singer Akosia Sabet,
Bast returns to the MCU for the first time

00:02:16.409 --> 00:02:18.260
since her premiere appearance.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.364
Knowing Kevin Feige's proclivity for Easter
eggs and callbacks, it's unlikely to be her last.

00:02:23.364 --> 00:02:24.780
"You never forget your first."

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.510
Her visage isn't as bombastic as some of the
deities seated around her, but her cat-eared

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.750
helmet and golden adornments still draw the
eye.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.390
Her appearance is brief, but her presence
cements director Taika Waititi's attention

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.470
to detail.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.330
Even though Thor is off-Earth going on his
own adventures, the moment reminds viewers

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.680
that the events of the film correlate to a
larger narrative.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.760
Within the Marvel canon, the panther goddess
has been worshiped since around 10,000 BC.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.159
Bast is an African deity that can take a male
or female form.

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:58.680
As the source of the magic that imbues the
Black Panther with their powers, Bast is revered

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.680
in Wakanda.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.480
In the comics, the late King T'Challa's sister
Shuri takes the opportunity to stand before

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.280
Bast, though she is deemed too immature to
become the next Black Panther.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:13.340
However, Shuri does eventually take up the
mantle and become queen of Wakanda, a journey

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.680
that could be utilized for the upcoming film
adaptation.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.959
Whether or not "Wakanda Forever" makes use
of that particular storyline, it makes sense

00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:24.390
that the panther goddess would play some kind
of role in the narrative.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:28.849
Bast's existence in Omnipotent City could
also hint at what's to come in Phase Four.

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:34.239
The goddess also has ties to Victor von Doom,
who will ultimately become Dr. Doom, and Reed

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:38.590
Richards, whose appearance in "Doctor Strange
in the Multiverse of Madness" could be teasing

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.299
a classic Marvel Comics storyline called "Secret
Wars."

00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:46.849
Bast is also the half-sibling to the god Khonshu
from "Moon Knight," a connection that provides

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:51.584
an opportunity for Marvel to flesh out the
minor characters it's introduced over the years.

00:03:51.584 --> 00:03:56.640
Whatever it means for the big picture, Bast's
appearance is a fun detail to look out for

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.379
whenever you catch "Thor: Love and Thunder."

